Open shell menus and panels through Hyprland global shortcuts.

Backport of Omarchy pull request #13418 (merged into quattro as 6762769b)
onto the pinned 4.0.4 tree (c668141e). Super+Space and the other menu and
panel bindings ran omarchy-menu or omarchy-shell, which start a qs IPC
client that omarchy-shell kills on its timeout; a killed client loses the
toggle or delivers it late. The shell now registers a Hyprland global
shortcut for each entry in default/omarchy/shortcuts, and the bindings
dispatch it with hl.dsp.global, so a keypress starts no process.

Only the clipboard.lua hunk differs from upstream: its context lines follow
the pinned tree's universal copy and paste bindings. Remove this patch once
the pinned Omarchy includes 6762769b.

